#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0261 expect=violation domain=ADAE
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when AEDECOD is not present in an ADVERSE EVENT sub-class OCCDS dataset (e.g., ADAE).
# Declared-tier pin: no column carries an OCCDS or ADVERSE EVENT signal, so both scope axes come
# from the structure= / subclass= declaration alone — the Define-XML def:Class / def:SubClass path.
# The declaration must reach RuleRunner as well as the scenario pre-gate; without it the rule is
# SKIPPED mid-execution and this scenario fails.
# The #define block is the mandatory carrier for the declaration: RuleRunner reads the declared
# tier from `defineProvider != null ? defineProvider : libraryProvider`, so the harness refuses a
# structure=/subclass= scenario with neither block rather than materialise an empty provider and
# silently disable that level's availability self-skips.
#define standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset ADAE structure=OCCDS subclass=AE
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015
---
